PHASE 18 — Referral System

Goal:
Build student referral links and reward tracking.

How it works:
1. Student gets referral code.
2. Student shares link.
3. Visitor lands with ?ref=CODE.
4. Referral code stored through checkout.
5. If payment is verified/approved, referral is recorded.
6. Owner manually applies reward.

Settings:
- Referral program enabled/disabled
- Reward type: free session / AED discount / both
- Reward value
- Terms text

Student pages:
- /student/referrals

Parent pages:
- /parent/referrals optional

Owner pages:
- /owner/referrals
- /owner/settings/referrals

Referral statuses:
- pending
- qualified
- reward_pending
- reward_applied
- rejected

Acceptance criteria:
- Student has referral code/link.
- Checkout stores referral code.
- Paid/verified order creates referral record.
- Owner can apply reward.
- Reward can add credit or discount record.
- Audit log records reward.

Manual test checklist:
- Copy referral link.
- Open public site with ref.
- Complete checkout.
- Mark payment paid.
- Confirm referral appears.
- Apply reward.

Stop condition:
Stop here. Test this phase before continuing.
